Ward C. Burrows writes:
>odlin@reed.edu (Iain Odlin) writes:
>>  Does anyone have any hints/tips/tricks regarding survival on the Elemental
>>  Planes?  

>You sense the presence of spoilers.--more--

Make sure to have a ring of levitation; this is useful for both the
fire and air levels.  Polypiling on the castle level (way back when)
to get AC -40 or so is also a good idea, as that extra AC considerably
reduces the damage you take from the occasional Archon.


>Carry a wand of secret door detection and a light source.  One zap of the 
>wand will make all traps close to you (including the portal) visible!

Another even better way is to detect the portal using a crystal ball.
(Apply it and look for '^'.)  If there are multiple traps found, use
'/' to look at them all to find the portal.  Then you teleport next to
it, and in the third move, you are out.  I used a wish to get the ball
after I was getting repeated crashes on the fire level; it was well
worth it.


>As for the plane
>of water, patience...patience...patience... the bubble will eventually take
>you to the portal, so you don't need to go outside it, and if you value your
>life, watch your step.  One misstep = death!!!

Furthermore, the portal will be shown on crystal ball as outside of
the bubble, but it doesn't seem to actually be there.  (I had the
magic breathing amulet so I tported over to check it out.)  Eventually
I found it in the air bubble.... moving away from me!  Had to chase it
down to jump in.

